      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T21:19:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This hook would allow vendor modules to skip the dm-verity check.  I think this is a great example of why vendor hooks in security-relevant components is a bad idea.\n\nPlease consider using the `try_verify_in_tasklet` option, which eliminates the dm-verity scheduling overhead in many cases, which seems to be what you\u0027re trying to achieve.  It was recently improved by the following commits:\n\n* FROMGIT: dm-verity: support block number limits for different ioprio classes\n* FROMGIT: dm-bufio: don\u0027t schedule in atomic context\n* FROMGIT: dm-verity: use softirq context only when !need_resched()\n\nAdditionally, please ensure your Android build includes https://r.android.com/q/topic:%22dm-verity-max-age-seconds%22, which fixed the Merkle tree block cache to not expire so quickly.\n\nIf there are remaining issues, please collaborate with us and upstream to fix them.",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "179354bb_4fbd7ddd",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1983857
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-26T03:31:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your advice:\nRegarding skipping dm-verity verification:\nIn our custom module, we ensure that dm-verity verification is always performed. Also skipping this check will not be intercepted by CTS/VTS tests.\n\nRegarding try_verify_in_tasklet:\nThis appears to trigger the queue_work(system_bh_wq, \u0026io-\u003ebh_work) logic in verity_end_io. We don’t fully understand the significance of system_bh_wq here: What makes this workqueue special, and how does it improve performance?",
      "parentUuid": "8cf096a2_738bab13",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e8bd11f_4e24775d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1983857
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-26T03:46:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding our previous discussion, our verity_end_io executes in a hard interrupt context.",
      "parentUuid": "179354bb_4fbd7ddd",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "612f959b_3ce0e3ac",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-26T21:19:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`system_bh_wq` is the bottom-half (BH) workqueue.  It causes the work to be executed in softirq context, also known as BH context.  If `verity_end_io` is being called in hardirq context on your devices, what this means is that (if `try_verify_in_tasklet` is set) when that hardirq finishes, the CPU will immediately execute a softirq that does the verity work.  There\u0027s no scheduling overhead.\n\nTo reduce impact on real-time tasks, the latest implementation of `try_verify_in_tasklet` chooses softirq context only when the I/O request is 8 KiB or less and rescheduling of the current task has not been requested yet.  Note that 4 KiB is a common request size, and the latency of it is very important, as it\u0027s what the kernel uses for synchronous reads.  Additionally, hashing 4 KiB with the ARMv8 crypto extensions takes only a few microseconds.  So this solution should work rather well.  We have other partners who are either already using or considering using this solution.\n\nSo, can you consider this solution, which is already upstream as well as already in this kernel branch?  There\u0027s no need for a vendor hook if you just use that.",
      "parentUuid": "0e8bd11f_4e24775d",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "005e87f0_3431381f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1983857
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-27T14:04:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027ve conducted practical tests on the impact of enabling try_verify_in_tasklet. It appears that even when there are numerous softirqs, this approach cannot guarantee that the verity processing occurs within the softirq context. In such scenarios, the scheduling overhead does not seem to outperform our optimized solution.\n\nAdditionally, older kernel versions don\u0027t have the system_bh_wq. We would like to address/optimize the scheduling overhead for this verity processing on devices running these kernels as well.",
      "parentUuid": "612f959b_3ce0e3ac",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82f944ae_1fb956d5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-27T20:07:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We\u0027ve conducted practical tests on the impact of enabling try_verify_in_tasklet. It appears that even when there are numerous softirqs, this approach cannot guarantee that the verity processing occurs within the softirq context. In such scenarios, the scheduling overhead does not seem to outperform our optimized solution.\n\nWas your test done on the latest version of `try_verify_in_tasklet`, and if so what threshold did you use for the I/O size?  It could be tuned to use softirq context in more cases, but it\u0027s meant to be balanced to avoid too much impact on other tasks.  It\u0027s important not to optimize for one part of the system (dm-verity) at the expense of everything else.\n\n\u003e Additionally, older kernel versions don\u0027t have the system_bh_wq. We would like to address/optimize the scheduling overhead for this verity processing on devices running these kernels as well.\n\nWe\u0027d be glad to backport patches from upstream if needed.\n\nAlso, please let me know if you\u0027ve incorporated https://r.android.com/q/topic:%22dm-verity-max-age-seconds%22 as I suggested.",
      "parentUuid": "005e87f0_3431381f",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eda6cd0_99a2a05c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1983857
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-30T02:32:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I conducted the tests based on the 6.12 kernel, incorporating the changes you mentioned. The threshold used was the default: #define DM_VERITY_USE_BH_DEFAULT_BYTES 8192.\n\n\"It\u0027s important not to optimize for one part of the system (dm-verity) at the expense of everything else,\"We fully agree that system optimizations should not disproportionately impact other component，and based on current tests, we believe using our own scheduling policy can also ensure this principle.\n\nAnother reason we proposed this vendorhook is: we don\u0027t intend to prioritize all verity operations. Instead, we\u0027ll use our internal logic to determine which specific cases require high-priority handling.\n\n\"We\u0027d be glad to backport patches from upstream if needed,\" are you suggesting backporting the entire system_bh_wq mechanism to older kernel versions? That would require a significant amount of work...",
      "parentUuid": "82f944ae_1fb956d5",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c90af46a_35ede015",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-30T19:03:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Regarding skipping dm-verity verification:\nIn our custom module, we ensure that dm-verity verification is always performed. Also skipping this check will not be intercepted by CTS/VTS tests.\n\nI certainly hope you don\u0027t skip it, but my point is that this hook would easily allow any vendor/OEM to skip the check.  I worry about people using it to disable security checks to gain a performance advantage.  As far as I know, and as you mentioned yourself, there are no CTS or VTS tests that would detect this.  It seems like a bad idea.\n\n\u003e Another reason we proposed this vendorhook is: we don\u0027t intend to prioritize all verity operations. Instead, we\u0027ll use our internal logic to determine which specific cases require high-priority handling.\n\ntry_verify_in_tasklet already takes into account the I/O priority.  If you found that the logic isn\u0027t sufficient, could you propose an improvement to it?\n\n\u003e \"We\u0027d be glad to backport patches from upstream if needed,\" are you suggesting backporting the entire system_bh_wq mechanism to older kernel versions? That would require a significant amount of work...\n\nI\u0027d be willing to backport the BH workqueue if needed.  However, this is irrelevant to this CL, since this CL is for android16-6.12 which already has it.",
      "parentUuid": "9eda6cd0_99a2a05c",
      "revId": "2670a45b1745c116d2d61c70d591b9495cb86cd5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
